# Keyboard shortcuts for new users of the desktop shell (V3 of the working brief).
# Installed to /etc/skel/.config/kglobalshortcutsrc by the kuura-shell package
# (docs/SHELL_CONTRACT.md). Bound to the STOCK components that stand in for the
# future bespoke Beacon/Shelf/Overview surfaces, matching the screenshot harness's
# states (docs/HARNESS_CONTRACT.md, harness/states.toml): search -> the stock
# KRunner; window overview -> the stock Overview effect; close/hide window and
# switch workspace -> KWin's own existing shortcut components.
#
# Component and action names below are copied VERBATIM from the guest image's own
# live default (`cat ~/.config/kglobalshortcutsrc` in a freshly booted, never
# customised session, KWin 6.7.5-1 / kglobalaccel 6.30.0-1) - not invented. KDE's
# global-shortcut daemon (kglobalaccel; it runs as a module of kded6 in this build,
# there is no standalone kglobalacceld process) merges these values in at its own
# start-up, overriding each owning component's compiled-in default for the actions
# named here; every other action a component registers keeps its own default.
#
# ---- Left out on purpose: KRunner's own search shortcut, the Overview shortcut ----
# Both already have a correct, verified-firing default with no file needed at all:
# KRunner's own default is Alt+Space / Alt+F2 (read from its shipped
# /usr/share/kglobalaccel/org.kde.krunner.desktop: X-KDE-Shortcuts=Alt+Space,Alt+F2);
# the Overview effect's own default is Meta+W (read from the [kwin] group of the
# live dump: "Overview=Meta+W,Meta+W,Toggle Overview"). Both are already relied on by
# harness/states.toml's "search-open" and "overview" states today, unmodified, so
# they demonstrably fire already. KRunner's own kglobalshortcutsrc GROUP name could
# NOT be confirmed live in the time available (it never materialises in the file
# until a user actually customises it away from the default, and introspecting
# org.kde.kglobalaccel's D-Bus tree only confirmed the D-BUS OBJECT PATH segment
# "org_kde_krunner_desktop", which is not necessarily the exact ini group spelling).
# Rather than guess a plausible-sounding group name for a shortcut that already
# works, it is left alone; do not add a [krunner]/[org.kde.krunner...] override here
# without confirming the real group name live first.
#
# ---- [kwin] component: close, minimize, switch desktop ----
# Window Close / Window Minimize: this is ALREADY the compiled default (Alt+F4 /
# Meta+PgDown, confirmed in the same live dump) - pinned explicitly here only so a
# future KDE point release cannot silently change it from under this project, the
# same reasoning harness/vm/guest/skel ships a complete layout instead of a
# generated one.
# Switch to Next Desktop / Switch to Previous Desktop: these two actions exist in
# the live dump but ship completely UNBOUND by default ("...=none,none,..."). Chose
# Ctrl+Alt+Right/Left: confirmed by inspecting the full live default dump that no
# other default shortcut anywhere uses this chord (Meta+Ctrl+Left/Right, a different
# chord, is already used by "Switch One Desktop to the Left/Right", the grid-relative
# variant of desktop switching - left untouched), and it matches the chord users
# coming from other desktops already expect for workspace switching.
#
# ---- Verification note (read before assuming this needs redoing) ----
# kglobalaccel seeds its live shortcut-to-action map once, when each owning
# component (kwin, for every action below) first registers its actions at its own
# start-up. Proven live: editing this file in an ALREADY-RUNNING session, then
# toggling org.kde.KGlobalAccel.blockGlobalShortcuts, then even killing and
# relaunching kded6 (the process that hosts kglobalaccel) did NOT change the live
# Ctrl+Alt+Right/Left binding - because kwin itself, the component that actually owns
# these actions, was never restarted, and a config-file edit alone does not push a
# new binding into an already-registered live QAction. The correct live-apply path
# is kglobalaccel's own org.kde.KGlobalAccel.setShortcut D-Bus method (confirmed to
# exist via introspection: `qdbus6 org.kde.kglobalaccel /kglobalaccel`), which is
# what the Shortcuts KCM itself calls instead of editing this file directly.
# For the real deployment case this skel file is for - a genuinely fresh user
# session - kwin, plasmashell and kglobalaccel all start cold together and read this
# file once at start-up, so every binding below applies from first login with no
# reload needed. Window Close/Minimize were confirmed against the live compiled
# default (so they are known-good). The two desktop-switch bindings were confirmed
# to be real, currently-unbound, collision-free kwin actions and written in the
# file format every other line in the live dump uses, but could NOT be hot-verified
# firing inside an already-running test session for the reason above - re-check them
# on a genuinely fresh boot (or via the Shortcuts KCM's own apply path) before
# relying on this as fully proven.
[kwin]
Window Close=Alt+F4,Alt+F4,Close Window
Window Minimize=Meta+PgDown,Meta+PgDown,Minimize Window
Switch to Next Desktop=Ctrl+Alt+Right,Ctrl+Alt+Right,Switch to Next Desktop
Switch to Previous Desktop=Ctrl+Alt+Left,Ctrl+Alt+Left,Switch to Previous Desktop
